  "body": "Hi,\r\nI've just upgrade Synapse version to 0.99 today but when I open link in browser:\r\nhttps://matrix.abc.com/_matrix/client/versions\r\nIt shows me:\r\n{\"versions\": [\"r0.0.1\", \"r0.1.0\", \"r0.2.0\", \"r0.3.0\"], \"unstable_features\": {\"m.lazy_load_members\": true}}\r\n\r\nWhen I use command:\r\ncurl -kv https://matrix.abc.com/_matrix/client/versions 2>&1 | grep \"Server:\"\r\nit shows me:\r\n< Server: nginx/1.14.0 (Ubuntu)\r\n\r\nBut is look I'm on latest version as:\r\n\r\nroot@:/home/mxadmin# dpkg -s matrix-synapse-py3 | grep '^Version:'\r\nVersion: 0.99.0+bionic1\r\n\r\nroot@:/home/mxadmin# dpkg -s matrix-synapse | grep '^Version:'\r\ndpkg-query: package 'matrix-synapse' is not installed and no information is available\r\nUse dpkg --info (= dpkg-deb --info) to examine archive files,\r\nand dpkg --contents (= dpkg-deb --contents) to list their contents.\r\n\r\nCould you advise how to check the version? Or I just didn't upgrade the matrix correctly?\r\n\r\nI have Ubuntu 18.04 and using just repository.",
